.TH SSMCP 1 "2026-11-16" "ssmcp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssmcp \- expose a local terminal through an SSH-authenticated MCP gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssmcp
.RB [ \-F " ssh_config" ]
.RB [ \-i " identity" ]
.RB [ \-p " port" ]
.RB [ \-\-shell " path" ]
.I user@host
.SH DESCRIPTION
ssmcp authenticates to OpenSSH using a public key and creates a new local
pseudo-terminal. The server returns an HTTPS MCP URL and a connection-scoped
bearer secret. One JSON object containing url and secret is written to standard
output. Diagnostics are written to standard error.
.PP
Keep the program running while the terminal is in use. Ctrl-C or SIGTERM closes
the SSH connection and terminal. The server revokes the URL and bearer secret.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-F " file"
Use a separate OpenSSH client configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-i " file"
Use the specified private key. ssh-agent is also supported.
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Connect to the specified SSH port.
.TP
.BI \-\-shell " path"
Run the specified absolute shell path in the local pseudo-terminal.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
The client permits only SSH public-key authentication. Standard OpenSSH host-key
verification remains enabled. The secret authorizes command execution with the
permissions of the local user for the lifetime of the connection.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
Default OpenSSH client configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/known_hosts
Trusted SSH host keys.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssmcpd (8),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
